From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:37:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 156/158] input: misc: egis-et5xx-ctrl: report the sensor type
 at probe like stock

Samsung's stock kernel is built without CONFIG_SENSORS_FPRINT_SECURE, so
its et5xx-spi driver checks the sensor over SPI at boot and reports
"egis" (3) in type_check, which the vendor HAL reads before it issues any
ioctl. The bus is the secure world's here; trust the device tree instead:
a named Egis chip reports "egis" from probe. Without a chipid the type
stays unknown, and the HAL can still override it with FP_SET_SENSOR_TYPE.

Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit bbf41a65f9f73cdc98751e96b05877b2a5e4d922)
---
 drivers/input/misc/egis-et5xx-ctrl.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/egis-et5xx-ctrl.c b/drivers/input/misc/egis-et5xx-ctrl.c
index 18c98eb7e..151c96608 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/egis-et5xx-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/egis-et5xx-ctrl.c
@@ -360,9 +360,18 @@ static int et5xx_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	fp->dev = dev;
 	mutex_init(&fp->lock);
 	init_waitqueue_head(&fp->waitq);
-	fp->sensortype = SENSOR_UNKNOWN;
-	if (of_property_read_string(dev->of_node, "egistec,chipid", &fp->chipid))
+	/*
+	 * Samsung's stock kernel probes the sensor over SPI at boot and reports
+	 * "egis" in type_check, which the vendor HAL reads before anything
+	 * else. The bus is the secure world's here, so trust the device tree:
+	 * a named Egis chip reports "egis"; the HAL can still override it.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_string(dev->of_node, "egistec,chipid", &fp->chipid)) {
 		fp->chipid = "ET5XX";
+		fp->sensortype = SENSOR_UNKNOWN;
+	} else {
+		fp->sensortype = SENSOR_EGIS;
+	}
 
 	fp->reset = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
 	if (IS_ERR(fp->reset))
